# TODO - Malbolge layout and encoding backend

## Objective

Implement address-sensitive instruction layout, self-modification planning,
encoding, jumps, data placement, runtime linkage, and final `.malbolge`
emission.

## Acceptance

- Layout solves address-sensitive decode and self-modification constraints
  reproducibly and emits only verifier-accepted `.malbolge` for the declared
  profile.
- The backend may additionally emit an annotated human/debug view, but
  canonicalizing that view must reproduce the executable `.malbolge` stream
  byte-for-byte; comments and layout never occupy target positions.
- The stage has deterministic input/output form, rejects malformed or
  unsupported input explicitly, and preserves source/profile provenance needed
  downstream.
- The declared scope contains no unresolved placeholder implementation or
  undocumented workaround required for this objective to function.
- Evidence is durable enough to move this TODO to `docs/todo/completed/` and
  remove the exact TODO heading without losing unfinished intent.

## Evidence

- First executable source-emission slice now lives under
  `src/compiler/malbolge-layout/`. It accepts only closed straight-line
  profile-bound sequences of no-op, machine byte I/O and halt operations,
  assigns exact code addresses starting at zero, and inverts the canonical
  VM decoder at every position without duplicating `XLAT1`. It requires a
  unique graphical source cell, a single final halt, two to 4096 cells, and
  independently re-admits the complete result against canonical profile ID,
  fingerprint and decoded operations before publication.
- Real `ProfileMachine` integration checks source admission, input/output,
  exact-step halt and all 94 encoding phases under both historical and current
  profiles. Tampered bytes/profile identities, missing/early halts and invalid
  lengths reject explicitly. This is valid machine code but **not** C-to-
  Malbolge lowering: data placement, nonlinear control flow, code-state
  transitions, guest runtime linkage and general ternary-IR realization remain
  unsupported.
- Expected durable artifact surface: `compiler/`, `src/`, `tests/compiler/`.
- Required evidence: golden/round-trip or normalized stage fixtures,
  deterministic hashes where promised, and end-to-end lowering regression cases.
- Prerequisite completion evidence: `ternary-machine-lowering`,
  `canonical-malbolge-target-profile`.
